@@ -0,0 +1,73 @@
+# Sampler request admission hook
+
+Scope: add an optional trusted, nonserialized request veto immediately before
+both sampler HTTP execution calls. This does not qualify native hard token or
+USD limits, enable Foreman dispatch, or introduce a resource ledger.
+
+1. Add deterministic local HTTP tests for streaming and nonstreaming denial,
+   absent-hook behavior, config/client clones, retry classification, safe
+   descriptors, and reason serialization.
+2. Add the inert public interface and closed error types needed to compile the
+   tests. Observe behavioral failure before adding execution checks.
+3. Invoke the hook at both HTTP execution points; preserve typed refusal across
+   error mirrors and classify it as terminal in sampler and shell recovery.
+4. Run targeted tests and the sampler suite, format the touched Rust files, and
+   inspect the diff. Report any wider workspace compilation limits separately.
+
+The descriptor contains only transport kind and optional exact encoded body
+length/BLAKE3 digest. It contains no headers, URL, credentials, or body content.
+The synchronous hook must make a bounded local decision without blocking or
+network I/O. Its opaque shared wrapper does not call the implementer's Debug.
+
+Config/client cloning preserves the same hook. Serialization deliberately drops
+it. Hosts must attach it again after deserialization. The shell preserves an
+existing hook during in-memory configuration reconstruction. CLI and ACP startup
+do not install a trusted authority. Startup, auxiliary clients, account identity,
+redirects, replays, exact tokenization, server-side work, billing reservations,
+and cross-process totals remain unqualified.
+
+Approval: host reviewed this scope and interface before implementation.
+
+## Initial sampler verification
+
+The tests were added before the execution checks. After adding inert interface
+types, the targeted run completed with 3 passed and 5 failed: both HTTP paths
+still sent requests, no descriptors reached the hook, and the actor entered
+retry backoff. After adding the checks, all 8 admission tests passed.
+
+`cargo +1.94.0 test -p xai-grok-sampler --locked --offline -j4` passed:
+255 unit tests and 41 integration tests. This result predates the shell
+propagation changes below. It does not establish whole-workspace acceptance.
+
+## Shell and pager corrections
+
+The shell completion payload preserves `message`, `error_kind`, and the closed
+denial `reason`. Admission denial remains terminal before compaction or salvage.
+The pager displays a terminal refusal even when an unrelated HTTP status suggests
+retry or compaction. The host verified these regressions before propagation work.
+
+## In-memory propagation candidate
+
+SessionActor captures the existing hook at spawn and preserves it during config
+reconstruction. Model rebuilds, subagent overrides, and session-local auxiliary
+sampler configurations clone the same authority. Catalog configurations retain
+`None`. Serialization cannot create authority or reset its resource allowance.
+
+Sol observed four missing-hook regression failures before wiring the clones.
+Sol then reported four passing regressions and a successful full CLI compilation
+check. The host independently ran the shell `admission` test filter: 18 tests
+passed, including all four propagation tests and both denial regressions.
+The host also completed `cargo +1.94.0 check -p xai-grok-pager-bin --locked --offline -j4` successfully.
+The host reran the full sampler suite after propagation: 255 unit tests and
+41 integration tests passed. All native checks used Rust 1.94.0 and pinned
+Protobuf 29.3 with locked, offline dependencies.
+The tests use a weak reference to distinguish preserved authority from
+a replacement object.
+
+## Remaining coverage gaps
+
+Context metrics call `/tokenize-text` through a direct HTTP client. Those counts
+exclude complete request serialization and do not establish exact token bounds.
+Web-search clients call `/responses` outside the sampler. These paths need
+qualified resource boundaries before live dispatch. Hook propagation alone does
+not establish coverage of every native request. Foreman must remain closed.
